    "https://jobs.nccu.edu/postings/38527": {
      "title": "Clinical Instructor - Real Estate / Director of Real Estate Studies",
      "description": "North Carolina Central University Applicant Portal | Clinical Instructor - Real Estate / Director of Real Estate Studies Skip to Main Content Toggle navigation Home Search Jobs Log In /Create Account Help Benefits Clery Report Equal Employment Opportunity Clinical Instructor - Real Estate / Director of Real Estate Studies Bookmark this Posting Print Preview | Apply for this Job Please see Special Instructions for more details. Final candidates are subject to criminal background checks, and education/license verification prior to employment. Posting Details To create a Posting, first complete the information on this screen, then click the Next button or select the page in the left hand navigation menu. Proceed through all sections and complete all necessary information. To submit the Posting to the next approval step, you must go to the Posting Summary page by clicking on the Next button until you reach the Summary page, or you can select the Summary page link from the left navigation menu. Once the Summary page appears, hover your mouse over the orange Take Action on Posting button for a list of possible approval step options. Position Information Working Title Clinical Instructor - Real Estate / Director of Real Estate Studies Position Number F611035 Appointment Type Fixed Term: 1 year FTE 1=9/10 month -Faculty only Position Overview Be an Eagle - Where Purpose Takes Flight! Are you ready to make an impact? At North Carolina Central University ( NCCU ), we are more than an institution—we are a community rooted in a legacy of excellence and transformation. A historically Black university located in Durham, North Carolina, also known as ‘The City of Medicine,’ NCCU has been a cornerstone of education since 1910, fostering innovation and progress. Join our team and enjoy a comprehensive benefits package and exclusive perks designed to support your work-life balance. At NCCU , your professional growth will be nurtured, and your contributions will help shape the future for our students and the community we serve. Become part of a legacy that drives change and achievement. An opportunity awaits you at NCCU , where your purpose can take flight. Visit NCCU .edu . Primary Function of Organizational Unit North Carolina Central University ( NCCU is a Historically Black College or University ( HBCU ) with a mission to prepare students to succeed in the global marketplace. We are consistently ranked as a top HBCU in the South by U.S News & World Report. NCCU Business is a flagship program with majors in Accounting, Business Management (Finance, Human Resources, Marketing, Management, Real Estate, and Entrepreneurship) Computer Information Systems, Information Technology (Data Analytics, CyberSecurity, and Information Communications Technology), and Hospitality & Tourism Administration. We offer BBA and MBA degrees within the School of Business. Our Program is accredited by AACSB , considered the gold standard. NCCU’S School of Business has an enrollment of over 1,200 students in its undergraduate and graduate programs. The department has faculty members who have published in peer-reviewed journals. Additional information about the School of Business is available at: http://www.nccu.edu/academics/sc/business/index.cfm. Primary Purpose of Position The School of Business at North Carolina Central University seeks highly qualified applicants for a 9-month, Clinical Instructor of Real Estate who will also serve as Director of the Real Estate Studies. The successful candidate will teach undergraduate and graduate courses in Real Estate and related business disciplines while providing strategic leadership for the Real Estate Studies through the development and administration of innovative academic, co-curricular, and community engagement initiatives that promote Real Estate, innovation, and economic development. The qualified candidate must have earned Ph.D. in Real Estate or a related field from an AACSB -accredited program or an equally relevant accredited program in a related discipline. Candidates with a Master’s degree and significant working experience in the real estate area will also be considered. The Director will work collaboratively with faculty, students, alumni, corporate partners, community organizations, and governmental agencies to advance the mission and strategic goals of the School of Business and the University. Required Knowledge, Skills, and Abilities Responsibilities include teaching undergraduate and graduate courses in real estate and related business disciplines. Faculty will engage students in the study and application of , and economic development through experiential learning and applied business practices. While the School’s primary focus is teaching, maintenance of academic qualifications includes continuous scholarly productivity in discipline-related quality journals and/or sustained professional engagement consistent with AACSB standards. Service activities include selected committee assignments at the departmental, School, and/or University levels. The successful candidate must demonstrate excellent oral, written, and interpersonal communication skills; effective problem-solving, diplomacy, and leadership abilities; a demonstrated ability to work collaboratively and develop productive relationships with students, faculty, alumni, entrepreneurs, industry partners, and community stakeholders; and a commitment to maintaining high professional standards and integrity. The candidate should also possess the ability to develop and manage real estate programs, foster innovation, secure external partnerships and funding opportunities, and provide strategic leadership for the Real Estate Program. Minimum Education/Experience The qualified candidate must have earned Ph.D. in Real Estate or a related field from an AACSB accredited program or an equally relevant accredited program in a related discipline. Candidates with a Master’s degree and significant working experience in the real estate area will also be considered. Licenses or Certification required by Statute or Regulation N/A Equal Opportunity Employer North Carolina Central University is an equal opportunity and affirmative action employer. All qualified applicants will receive consideration for employment without regard to age, color, disability, gender, gender expression, gender identity, genetic information, national origin, race, religion, sex, sexual orientation, or status as a protected veteran. Key Responsibilities and Related Competencies Function Instructional Describe the specific tasks and responsibilities related to the function. Faculty will focus on teaching, scholarly engagement, service, and alignment with the mission of the School of Business. Primary teaching responsibilities include undergraduate and graduate courses in Real Estate and related business disciplines. Responsibilities include teaching in face-to-face and online environments, advising and mentoring students, participating in curriculum development and assessment activities, and maintaining academic qualifications through continuous scholarly and professional engagement Function Administrative Describe the specific tasks and responsibilities related to the function. Serve as Director of the Real Estate Studies by providing strategic vision and leadership for the program; developing and expanding real estate programming across the University; fostering innovation and a real estate ownership among students, faculty, and the community; building partnerships with industry, government, nonprofit organizations, and alumni; managing external grants and donor-supported initiatives; organizing real estate competitions, workshops, incubator activities ,and outreach programs; coordinating advisory board activities; pursuing external funding opportunities; representing the real estate program at university and community events; and ensuring effective administration of the program in support of the School’s strategic priorities. Function Public Service Describe the specific tasks and responsibilities related to the function. Provide service to the School, University, profession, and community through committee participation, professional engagement, community outreach, mentorship, and activities that advance entrepreneurship, economic development, and the mission of North Carolina Central University. Posting Detail Information Posting Number F000321 Open Date 10/15/2026 Close Date Open Until Filled No Date Position Available 07/01/2027 Special Instructions to Applicants Final candidates are subject to criminal background checks, and education/license verification prior to employment. Applicant Documents Required Documents Resume/CV Cover Letter Unofficial Transcripts (official required from selected candidate) List of References Optional Documents Other Document DD-214 (Veterans Only) Licenses and/or Certification required by Statute or Regulation Supplemental Questions Required fields are indicated with an asterisk (*). North Carolina Central University 1801 Fayetteville St. Durham, NC, 27707 Mainline: 919-530-6100 The Clery Act Privacy Policy Title IX © 2025 North Carolina Central University To ensure the security of your data, you will be logged out due to inactivity in 3 minutes at . Any data not saved will be lost. Click 'OK' to keep your session active."
    },
    "https://jobs.nccu.edu/postings/38523": {
      "title": "Director of Law Library",
      "description": "North Carolina Central University Applicant Portal | Director of Law Library Skip to Main Content Toggle navigation Home Search Jobs Log In /Create Account Help Benefits Clery Report Equal Employment Opportunity Director of Law Library Bookmark this Posting Print Preview | Apply for this Job Please see Special Instructions for more details. Final candidates are subject to criminal background checks, and education/license verification prior to employment. Posting Details To create a Posting, first complete the information on this screen, then click the Next button or select the page in the left hand navigation menu. Proceed through all sections and complete all necessary information. To submit the Posting to the next approval step, you must go to the Posting Summary page by clicking on the Next button until you reach the Summary page, or you can select the Summary page link from the left navigation menu. Once the Summary page appears, hover your mouse over the orange Take Action on Posting button for a list of possible approval step options. Position Information Working Title Director of Law Library Position Number F611152 Appointment Type Tenure Track - Initial 2 years FTE 1 = 40 hours/week, 12 months Position Overview Be an Eagle - Where Purpose Takes Flight! Are you ready to make an impact? At North Carolina Central University ( NCCU ), we are more than an institution—we are a community rooted in a legacy of excellence and transformation. A historically Black university located in Durham, North Carolina, also known as ‘The City of Medicine,’ NCCU has been a cornerstone of education since 1910, fostering innovation and progress. Join our team and enjoy a comprehensive benefits package and exclusive perks designed to support your work-life balance. At NCCU , your professional growth will be nurtured, and your contributions will help shape the future for our students and the community we serve. Become part of a legacy that drives change and achievement. An opportunity awaits you at NCCU , where your purpose can take flight. Visit NCCU .edu . Primary Function of Organizational Unit The NCCU School of Law Library provides information services and resources that promote the performance of high-quality legal research activities by our faculty, students, staff and community. The law library reference department has primary responsibility for providing legal research instruction and reference services to students, faculty, alumni and public patrons. Primary Purpose of Position The Law Library Director provides leadership and oversight of the Law Library’s operations, resources, personnel, and services in support of the School of Law’s academic mission. Required Knowledge, Skills, and Abilities 1. Comprehensive knowledge of legal research methods, legal information resources, law library operations, and emerging research technologies. 2. Knowledge of law school accreditation standards and professional standards applicable to academic law libraries. 3. Demonstrated ability to provide strategic leadership and effectively manage library personnel, operations, budgets, collections, and services. 4. Strong knowledge of electronic databases, digital resources, library technology, and information-management systems. 5. Ability to develop, evaluate, and implement policies, procedures, programs, and services that support the academic mission of the law school. 6. Strong teaching and instructional skills, including the ability to support legal research instruction and student development. 7. Excellent written, oral, interpersonal, and organizational communication skills. 8. Ability to collaborate effectively with faculty, students, administrators, staff, and external partners. 9. Demonstrated ability to supervise, mentor, and evaluate professional and support staff. 10. Ability to assess evolving legal education, research, technology, and library trends and implement appropriate innovations. 11.Strong analytical, problem-solving, planning, and decision-making skills. 12. Commitment to excellent service and supporting faculty scholarship, student learning, bar readiness, and professional preparation. Minimum Education/Experience MLS , JD required. Licenses or Certification required by Statute or Regulation MLS , JD required. Equal Opportunity Employer North Carolina Central University is an equal opportunity and affirmative action employer. All qualified applicants will receive consideration for employment without regard to age, color, disability, gender, gender expression, gender identity, genetic information, national origin, race, religion, sex, sexual orientation, or status as a protected veteran. Key Responsibilities and Related Competencies Function Instructional Describe the specific tasks and responsibilities related to the function. The Faculty will develop and design curriculum plans to foster learning, stimulate class discussions, and ensure student engagement. The Faculty will provide tutoring and academic counseling to students, maintain class related records, and assess student coursework. Maintain regularly scheduled office hours in order to advise and assist students. Function Research Describe the specific tasks and responsibilities related to the function. The Faculty will conduct research in a particular field of knowledge, and publish findings in professional journals, books, and/or electronic media. Collaborate with colleagues to address teaching and research issues. Keep abreast of developments in their field by reading current literature, talking with colleagues, and participate in professional conferences. Function Public Service Describe the specific tasks and responsibilities related to the function. Serve on various Law School and University committees that deal with institutional policies, departmental matters, and academic issues. Participate in campus and community events. Posting Detail Information Posting Number F000316 Open Date 10/01/2026 Close Date Open Until Filled No Date Position Available 07/01/2027 Special Instructions to Applicants Final candidates are subject to criminal background checks, and education/license verification prior to employment. Applicant Documents Required Documents Resume/CV Unofficial Transcripts (official required from selected candidate) List of References Optional Documents Cover Letter Other Document DD-214 (Veterans Only) NGB23A or NGB22/DD256 (National Guard Only) Licenses and/or Certification required by Statute or Regulation Supplemental Questions Required fields are indicated with an asterisk (*). North Carolina Central University 1801 Fayetteville St. Durham, NC, 27707 Mainline: 919-530-6100 The Clery Act Privacy Policy Title IX © 2025 North Carolina Central University To ensure the security of your data, you will be logged out due to inactivity in 3 minutes at . Any data not saved will be lost. Click 'OK' to keep your session active."
