 our students and the community we serve. Become part of a legacy that drives change and achievement. An opportunity awaits you at NCCU , where your purpose can take flight. Visit NCCU .edu . Primary Function of Organizational Unit The mission of the Department of Language and Literature at North Carolina Central University is to engage students in languages, cultures, literatures, linguistics, and writing. We foster students’ analytical and creative thinking, problem-solving abilities, and communication strategies to prepare students for their responsibilities in civic and professional life. Primary Purpose of Position To teach 1-3 in-person sections of Elementary Spanish I and/or II per semester To hold 4-8 office hours per week. Required Knowledge, Skills, and Abilities Demonstrated excellence in teaching Elementary Spanish in a face-to-face classroom. Minimum Education/Experience M.A. in Spanish or Romance Language Required; 18 hours minimum of graduate coursework in Spanish; Two years experience teaching Spanish at the university level. Licenses or Certification required by Statute or Regulation None Equal Opportunity Employer North Carolina Central University is an equal opportunity and affirmative action employer. All qualified applicants will receive consideration for employment without regard to age, color, disability, gender, gender expression, gender identity, genetic information, national origin, race, religion, sex, sexual orientation, or status as a protected veteran. Key Responsibilities and Related Competencies Posting Detail Information Posting Number F000314 Open Date 10/11/2026 Close Date 12/18/2026 Open Until Filled Yes Date Position Available 01/04/2027 Special Instructions to Applicants Required Documents Resume/CV Cover Letter Unofficial Transcripts (official required from selected candidate) List of References(Must have 3) Final candidates are subject to criminal background checks, and education/license verification prior to employment. Applicant Documents Required Documents Resume/CV Cover Letter Unofficial Transcripts (official required from selected candidate) Letter of Recommendation 1 Letter of Recommendation 2 Letter of Recommendation 3 List of References Optional Documents Other Document DD-214 (Veterans Only) Licenses and/or Certification required by Statute or Regulation Supplemental Questions Required fields are indicated with an asterisk (*). North Carolina Central University 1801 Fayetteville St. Durham, NC, 27707 Mainline: 919-530-6100 The Clery Act Privacy Policy Title IX © 2025 North Carolina Central University To ensure the security of your data, you will be logged out due to inactivity in 3 minutes at . Any data not saved will be lost. Click 'OK' to keep your session active."
