pe the future for our students and the community we serve. Become part of a legacy that drives change and achievement. An opportunity awaits you at NCCU , where your purpose can take flight. Visit NCCU .edu . Primary Function of Organizational Unit Are you ready to make an impact? At North Carolina Central University ( NCCU ), we are more than an institution—we are a community rooted in a legacy of excellence and transformation. A historically Black university located in Durham, North Carolina, also known as ‘The City of Medicine,’ NCCU has been a cornerstone of education since 1910, fostering innovation and progress. Primary Purpose of Position Teach in-person General Education Courses in Arts & Humanities. Hold 4-8 office hours per week. Participate in Faculty Development Sessions. Required Knowledge, Skills, and Abilities The position requires an emphasis on classroom management, the ability to teach classes of approximately 45 students, and participate in department meetings. Computer knowledge and willingness to participate in faculty development is essential. Use of technological platforms such as Canvas is required. Must be willing to communicate with students and manage a large combination lecture/discussion classroom. Minimum Education/Experience The applicant must hold a M.A. degree minimum. A minimum of 18 hours of graduate coursework in English, African-American Studies, or a related Humanities discipline required. Licenses or Certification required by Statute or Regulation No licenses or certification is required. Equal Opportunity Employer North Carolina Central University is an equal opportunity and affirmative action employer. All qualified applicants will receive consideration for employment without regard to age, color, disability, gender, gender expression, gender identity, genetic information, national origin, race, religion, sex, sexual orientation, or status as a protected veteran. Key Responsibilities and Related Competencies Posting Detail In