    "https://jobs.nccu.edu/postings/38317": {
      "title": "Assistant Professor",
      "description": "North Carolina Central University Applicant Portal | Assistant Professor Skip to Main Content Toggle navigation Home Search Jobs Log In /Create Account Help Benefits Clery Report Equal Employment Opportunity Assistant Professor Bookmark this Posting Print Preview | Apply for this Job Please see Special Instructions for more details. Final candidates are subject to criminal background checks, and education/license verification prior to employment. Posting Details To create a Posting, first complete the information on this screen, then click the Next button or select the page in the left hand navigation menu. Proceed through all sections and complete all necessary information. To submit the Posting to the next approval step, you must go to the Posting Summary page by clicking on the Next button until you reach the Summary page, or you can select the Summary page link from the left navigation menu. Once the Summary page appears, hover your mouse over the orange Take Action on Posting button for a list of possible approval step options. Position Information Working Title Assistant Professor Position Number F610197 Appointment Type Tenure Track - Initial 2 years FTE 1=9/10 month -Faculty only Position Overview Be an Eagle - Where Purpose Takes Flight! Are you ready to make an impact? At North Carolina Central University ( NCCU ), we are more than an institution—we are a community rooted in a legacy of excellence and transformation. A historically Black university located in Durham, North Carolina, also known as ‘The City of Medicine,’ NCCU has been a cornerstone of education since 1910, fostering innovation and progress. Join our team and enjoy a comprehensive benefits package and exclusive perks designed to support your work-life balance. At NCCU , your professional growth will be nurtured, and your contributions will help shape the future for our students and the community we serve. Become part of a legacy that drives change and achievement. An opportunity awaits you at NCCU , where your purpose can take flight. Visit NCCU .edu . Primary Function of Organizational Unit The NCCU School of Education offers undergraduate, graduate, licensure and professional development programs to train students to become teachers, principals, counselors, as well as serve as mentors to community schools. The School offers traditional, classroom-based instruction as well as synchronous and asynchronous online/web-based instruction. Faculty and staff offer diverse knowledge and experience, providing students with a unique learning experience using the latest technology; small class sizes provide easier access to peers and instructors. The primary goal of the School of Education is to prepare educators for Diverse Cultural Contexts in the 21st Century. Primary Purpose of Position This open rank, tenure-track faculty position is housed in the Special Education Program located in the Department of Curriculum and Instruction in the School of Education. Primary teaching responsibilities include face-to-face, hybrid, and online graduate courses in visual impairment, orientation and mobility, and related-areas. Supervision of clinical field experiences and research leading to publications and presentations at academic conferences is expected. Additional duties include academic advising, research and scholarship, university service, collaboration, accreditation related activities, promotion of the program and the university, and other duties as assigned by the department chair. Required Knowledge, Skills, and Abilities The successful candidate will have specific knowledge and experience in teaching undergraduate and graduate level courses and clinical supervision in Special Education with an emphasis in visual impairment and/or orientation and mobility. Candidates must demonstrate potential for effective teaching in special education at the graduate level, research and service, and activity in appropriate professional societies. Strong interpersonal skills, online education experience, and excellent organizational and communication skills are expected. Minimum Education/Experience Applicants must have an earned doctorate in Special Education or a related field with primary specialization in visual impairment and/or orientation and mobility. Candidates who are ABD will be considered. Candidate must have valid credentials in visual impairment and/or orientation and mobility. Applicants should have demonstrated potential for scholarly publication and successful teaching at the university level. Preference will be given to applicants committed to preparing teachers for culturally diverse populations, and those with expertise and teaching experience with PK-12 special education students with visual impairments. ACVREP Certification in the area of Orientation & Mobility and/or Assistive Technology. Licenses or Certification required by Statute or Regulation NC Teaching License or eligibility for NC Teaching License. Equal Opportunity Employer North Carolina Central University is an equal opportunity and affirmative action employer. All qualified applicants will receive consideration for employment without regard to age, color, disability, gender, gender expression, gender identity, genetic information, national origin, race, religion, sex, sexual orientation, or status as a protected veteran. Key Responsibilities and Related Competencies Function Instructional Describe the specific tasks and responsibilities related to the function. Effective teaching of campus and online classes in the special education program (i.e, visual impairment and orientation and mobility), supervision of practicum and internship. Engagement in curriculum development and support for accreditation maintenance. Function Research Describe the specific tasks and responsibilities related to the function. Visual impairment/orientation and mobility focused-research that leads to publication in peer reviewed journals and dissemination at state, national, and/or international conference. Procurement of grant funding that supports the mission of the School of Education. Function Administrative Describe the specific tasks and responsibilities related to the function. Student advisement and participation in school and university service, and scholarly activities. Scholarly activity includes contributions to the profession such as serving on the editorial board of a journal or as a member/leadership position of a state or national counseling organization. Posting Detail Information Posting Number F000301 Open Date 09/10/2026 Close Date Open Until Filled Yes Date Position Available 01/04/2027 Special Instructions to Applicants Final candidates are subject to criminal background checks, and education/license verification prior to employment. Applicant Documents Required Documents Resume/CV Unofficial Transcripts (official required from selected candidate) List of References Optional Documents Cover Letter Other Document DD-214 (Veterans Only) NGB23A or NGB22/DD256 (National Guard Only) Licenses and/or Certification required by Statute or Regulation Supplemental Questions Required fields are indicated with an asterisk (*). North Carolina Central University 1801 Fayetteville St. Durham, NC, 27707 Mainline: 919-530-6100 The Clery Act Privacy Policy Title IX © 2025 North Carolina Central University To ensure the security of your data, you will be logged out due to inactivity in 3 minutes at . Any data not saved will be lost. Click 'OK' to keep your session active."
    },
    "https://jobs.nccu.edu/postings/38273": {
      "title": "Clinical Professor of Public Administration",
      "description": "North Carolina Central University Applicant Portal | Clinical Professor of Public Administration Skip to Main Content Toggle navigation Home Search Jobs Log In /Create Account Help Benefits Clery Report Equal Employment Opportunity Clinical Professor of Public Administration Bookmark this Posting Print Preview | Apply for this Job Please see Special Instructions for more details. Final candidates are subject to criminal background checks, and education/license verification prior to employment. Posting Details To create a Posting, first complete the information on this screen, then click the Next button or select the page in the left hand navigation menu. Proceed through all sections and complete all necessary information. To submit the Posting to the next approval step, you must go to the Posting Summary page by clicking on the Next button until you reach the Summary page, or you can select the Summary page link from the left navigation menu. Once the Summary page appears, hover your mouse over the orange Take Action on Posting button for a list of possible approval step options. Position Information Working Title Clinical Professor of Public Administration Position Number F610759 Appointment Type Fixed Term: 3 year FTE 1=9/10 month -Faculty only Position Overview Be an Eagle - Where Purpose Takes Flight! Are you ready to make an impact? At North Carolina Central University ( NCCU ), we are more than an institution—we are a community rooted in a legacy of excellence and transformation. A historically Black university located in Durham, North Carolina, also known as ‘The City of Medicine,’ NCCU has been a cornerstone of education since 1910, fostering innovation and progress. Join our team and enjoy a comprehensive benefits package and exclusive perks designed to support your work-life balance. At NCCU , your professional growth will be nurtured, and your contributions will help shape the future for our students and the community we serve. Become part of a legacy that drives change and achievement. An opportunity awaits you at NCCU , where your purpose can take flight. Visit NCCU .edu . Primary Function of Organizational Unit The Department of Public Administration at North Carolina Central University is dedicated to preparing leaders for effective service in public and nonprofit sectors. Through rigorous instruction, innovative research, and community engagement, we equip students with the knowledge and skills necessary to address complex public management challenges, and foster a commitment to public service and community development. Primary Purpose of Position The Department of Public Administration at North Carolina Central University seeks a dynamic scholar-practitioner at the Clinical Professor level in this non-tenure-track faculty position. This faculty member will be a member of the core faculty of a NASPAA -accredited MPA Program. The successful candidate will play a crucial role in advancing our mission and preparing leaders for public service. We are particularly seeking individuals with expertise and a desire to contribute to our core course curriculum and elective course offerings. The primary responsibilities of this position encompass a range of academic activities essential to our department’s success. The candidate will teach core and elective courses in both face-to-face, hybrid and online formats, engage in scholarly and professional activity appropriate to the position, and provide mentorship and advising to our students. Additionally, this role will contribute to accreditation efforts, curriculum development, program assessment, and participate in community service initiatives, aligned with the core values of our department. The role also includes supervising internships, theses, and certifications, further enriching our students’ educational experience. This position is vital in upholding NCCU’s legacy as a premier Historically Black College and University ( HBCU ). The successful candidate will be instrumental in fostering an effective learning environment and preparing students to become transformative leaders in public administration. By contributing to our department’s teaching, research, and service goals, the faculty member will help shape the next generation of public servants while addressing critical issues facing underserved communities. Required Knowledge, Skills, and Abilities 1. Doctorate in Public Administration or a related field from an accredited institution. ( ABD Candidates: Degree must be awarded to be eligible for job offer.) 2. Demonstrated ability for achievement in teaching and research 3. Demonstrated capability to teach core public administration courses and electives. 4. Experience or capability in teaching both face-to-face and online courses. 5. Research experience with a record of scholarly publications in peer-reviewed journals. 6. Demonstrated ability or potential to secure external funding through grants, contracts, or other sources. 7. Commitment to mentoring and advising students, such as supervision of internships and theses. 8. Evidence of professional development, such as presentation of papers at professional meetings and involvement in professional organizations. 9. Ability to contribute to curriculum development and program assessment activities. 10. Strong communication and interpersonal skills, with the ability to work collaboratively with faculty, students, and external stakeholders. 11. Commitment to public service and community engagement. 12. Knowledge of, experience with, or demonstrated capacity to contribute substantially to professional accreditation processes, including program assessment and NASPAA standards. Minimum Education/Experience Earned doctorate in Public Administration, Public Policy, Political Science, or a closely related field from an accredited institution. Candidates must demonstrate a record of teaching, scholarship, and professional or academic service appropriate for appointment at the Clinical Professor level. Licenses or Certification required by Statute or Regulation NA Equal Opportunity Employer North Carolina Central University is an equal opportunity and affirmative action employer. All qualified applicants will receive consideration for employment without regard to age, color, disability, gender, gender expression, gender identity, genetic information, national origin, race, religion, sex, sexual orientation, or status as a protected veteran. Key Responsibilities and Related Competencies Function Instructional Describe the specific tasks and responsibilities related to the function. Teach core and elective courses in face-to-face, hybrid, and online formats Function Research Describe the specific tasks and responsibilities related to the function. Engage in active research and pursue external funding opportunities Function Administrative Describe the specific tasks and responsibilities related to the function. Contribute to curriculum development, program assessment, and mentoring and advising students, and other activities to support the functions of the department Function Public Service Describe the specific tasks and responsibilities related to the function. Participate in community service initiatives, relationship and capacity building, and outreach Posting Detail Information Posting Number F000303 Open Date 09/24/2026 Close Date Open Until Filled No Date Position Available 01/01/2027 Special Instructions to Applicants Final candidates are subject to criminal background checks, and education/license verification prior to employment. Applicant Documents Required Documents Resume/CV Cover Letter Unofficial Transcripts (official required from selected candidate) List of References Optional Documents Other Document DD-214 (Veterans Only) NGB23A or NGB22/DD256 (National Guard Only) Licenses and/or Certification required by Statute or Regulation Supplemental Questions Required fields are indicated with an asterisk (*). North Carolina Central University 1801 Fayetteville St. Durham, NC, 27707 Mainline: 919-530-6100 The Clery Act Privacy Policy Title IX © 2025 North Carolina Central University To ensure the security of your data, you will be logged out due to inactivity in 3 minutes at . Any data not saved will be lost. Click 'OK' to keep your session active."
    },
    "https://jobs.nccu.edu/postings/38272": {
      "title": "Associate Professor",
      "description": "North Carolina Central University Applicant Portal | Associate Professor Skip to Main Content Toggle navigation Home Search Jobs Log In /Create Account Help Benefits Clery Report Equal Employment Opportunity Associate Professor Bookmark this Posting Print Preview | Apply for this Job Please see Special Instructions for more details. Final candidates are subject to criminal background checks, and education/license verification prior to employment. Posting Details To create a Posting, first complete the information on this screen, then click the Next button or select the page in the left hand navigation menu. Proceed through all sections and complete all necessary information. To submit the Posting to the next approval step, you must go to the Posting Summary page by clicking on the Next button until you reach the Summary page, or you can select the Summary page link from the left navigation menu. Once the Summary page appears, hover your mouse over the orange Take Action on Posting button for a list of possible approval step options. Position Information Working Title Associate Professor Position Number F610474 Appointment Type Tenure Track - Initial 2 years FTE 1=9/10 month -Faculty only Position Overview Be an Eagle - Where Purpose Takes Flight! Are you ready to make an impact? At North Carolina Central University ( NCCU ), we are more than an institution—we are a community rooted in a legacy of excellence and transformation. A historically Black university located in Durham, North Carolina, also known as ‘The City of Medicine,’ NCCU has been a cornerstone of education since 1910, fostering innovation and progress. Join our team and enjoy a comprehensive benefits package and exclusive perks designed to support your work-life balance. At NCCU , your professional growth will be nurtured, and your contributions will help shape the future for our students and the community we serve. Become part of a legacy that drives change and achievement. An opportunity awaits you at NCCU , where your purpose can take flight. Visit NCCU .edu . Primary Function of Organizational Unit The primary purpose of the Department of Psychology is to provide undergraduate and graduate students rigorous training in the understanding of human behavior using scientific methods, and to provide students with the competencies, knowledge and skills sufficient to: (1) qualify for graduate/doctoral studies in psychology and the behavioral sciences and; (2) qualify for a range of human service positions that require the application of psychological or behavioral science methods and skills. Primary Purpose of Position The primary purpose of this faculty position is to teach in the undergraduate and/or the graduate programs, serve as an advisor, conduct research, engage in service to the unit, and contribute to the development of the Department of Psychology. Required Knowledge, Skills, and Abilities Licensed psychologist Ability to teach undergraduate courses and applied courses in the clinical concentration of the graduate program; supervise students on practicum; conduct research; serve as a thesis advisor in the graduate program Minimum Education/Experience Licensed psychologist and able to teach the applied courses in the Clinical Concentration of the graduate program and supervise students on practicum. Ph.D. Masters Licenses or Certification required by Statute or Regulation Licensed Psychologist/licensable in North Carolina Equal Opportunity Employer North Carolina Central University is an equal opportunity and affirmative action employer. All qualified applicants will receive consideration for employment without regard to age, color, disability, gender, gender expression, gender identity, genetic information, national origin, race, religion, sex, sexual orientation, or status as a protected veteran. Key Responsibilities and Related Competencies Function Instructional Describe the specific tasks and responsibilities related to the function. Teach undergraduate courses and graduate courses in the clinical concentration. Function Research Describe the specific tasks and responsibilities related to the function. Develop and conduct research. Publish peer reviewed journals. Function Administrative Describe the specific tasks and responsibilities related to the function. Performs academic and administrative duties, including developing and maintaining Canvas course shells, preparing and updating course syllabi, submitting grades and required academic documentation, maintaining student records, participating in department and college meetings, serving on committees, advising students, and completing other departmental and university administrative responsibilities as assigned. Function Other Duties as Assigned Describe the specific tasks and responsibilities related to the function. Other related administrative, instructional and service tasks as assigned by the department chair. Posting Detail Information Posting Number F000312 Open Date 09/23/2026 Close Date Open Until Filled No Date Position Available 01/01/2027 Special Instructions to Applicants Final candidates are subject to criminal background checks, and education/license verification prior to employment. Applicant Documents Required Documents Resume/CV Cover Letter Unofficial Transcripts (official required from selected candidate) Letter of Recommendation 1 Letter of Recommendation 2 Letter of Recommendation 3 List of References Optional Documents Other Document DD-214 (Veterans Only) NGB23A or NGB22/DD256 (National Guard Only) Licenses and/or Certification required by Statute or Regulation Supplemental Questions Required fields are indicated with an asterisk (*). North Carolina Central University 1801 Fayetteville St. Durham, NC, 27707 Mainline: 919-530-6100 The Clery Act Privacy Policy Title IX © 2025 North Carolina Central University To ensure the security of your data, you will be logged out due to inactivity in 3 minutes at . Any data not saved will be lost. Click 'OK' to keep your session active."
    },
    "https://jobs.nccu.edu/postings/38226": {
      "title": "Assistant/Associate/Full Professor",
      "description": "North Carolina Central University Applicant Portal | Assistant/Associate/Full Professor Skip to Main Content Toggle navigation Home Search Jobs Log In /Create Account Help Benefits Clery Report Equal Employment Opportunity Assistant/Associate/Full Professor Bookmark this Posting Print Preview | Apply for this Job Please see Special Instructions for more details. Criminal background required of selected candidate. Posting Details To create a Posting, first complete the information on this screen, then click the Next button or select the page in the left hand navigation menu. Proceed through all sections and complete all necessary information. To submit the Posting to the next approval step, you must go to the Posting Summary page by clicking on the Next button until you reach the Summary page, or you can select the Summary page link from the left navigation menu. Once the Summary page appears, hover your mouse over the orange Take Action on Posting button for a list of possible approval step options. Position Information Working Title Assistant/Associate/Full Professor Position Number F617042 Appointment Type Tenure Track - Initial 2 years FTE 1=9/10 month -Faculty only Position Overview Be an Eagle - Where Purpose Takes Flight! Are you ready to make an impact? At North Carolina Central University ( NCCU ), we are more than an institution—we are a community rooted in a legacy of excellence and transformation. A historically Black university located in Durham, North Carolina, also known as ‘The City of Medicine,’ NCCU has been a cornerstone of education since 1910, fostering innovation and progress. Join our team and enjoy a comprehensive benefits package and exclusive perks designed to support your work-life balance. At NCCU , your professional growth will be nurtured, and your contributions will help shape the future for our students and the community we serve. Become part of a legacy that drives change and achievement. An opportunity awaits you at NCCU , where your purpose can take flight. Visit NCCU .edu . Primary Function of Organizational Unit The North Carolina Central School of Law offers full-time day and part-time evening programs. The School of Law is committed to a policy that opposes discrimination on the basis of gender, age, race, religion, color, medical condition, handicap or disability, sexual orientation, national or ethnic origin in the administration of its educational policies, admissions policies, employment-related matters, financial aid programs, or other such University-administered programs. For more information, please visit the law school website at http://law.nccu.edu/. Primary Purpose of Position The faculty will teach courses in the discipline area of Law. Required Knowledge, Skills, and Abilities •Ability to design and teach courses at the J.D. level •Excellent oral and writing communication skills. •Excellent organizational and time management skills. •Excellent analytical skills. •Ability to work with a highly diverse staff, faculty, and student body. Minimum Education/Experience J.D. or equivalent legal degree required Licenses or Certification required by Statute or Regulation J.D. or equivalent legal degree required Equal Opportunity Employer North Carolina Central University is an equal opportunity and affirmative action employer. All qualified applicants will receive consideration for employment without regard to age, color, disability, gender, gender expression, gender identity, genetic information, national origin, race, religion, sex, sexual orientation, or status as a protected veteran. Key Responsibilities and Related Competencies Function Instructional Describe the specific tasks and responsibilities related to the function. The Faculty will develop and design curriculum plans to foster learning, stimulate class discussions, and ensure student engagement. The Faculty will provide tutoring and academic counseling to students, maintain class related records, and assess student coursework. Maintain regularly scheduled office hours in order to advise and assist students. Function Research Describe the specific tasks and responsibilities related to the function. The Faculty will conduct research in a particular field of knowledge, and publish findings in professional journals, books, and/or electronic media. Collaborate with colleagues to address teaching and research issues. Keep abreast of developments in their field by reading current literature, talking with colleagues, and participate in professional conferences. Function Public Service Describe the specific tasks and responsibilities related to the function. Serve on various Law School and University committees that deal with institutional policies, departmental matters, and academic issues. Participate in campus and community events. Posting Detail Information Posting Number F000305 Open Date 09/17/2026 Close Date Open Until Filled No Date Position Available 07/01/2027 Special Instructions to Applicants Criminal background required of selected candidate. Applicant Documents Required Documents Resume/CV Unofficial Transcripts (official required from selected candidate) List of References Optional Documents Other Document DD-214 (Veterans Only) Licenses and/or Certification required by Statute or Regulation Supplemental Questions Required fields are indicated with an asterisk (*). North Carolina Central University 1801 Fayetteville St. Durham, NC, 27707 Mainline: 919-530-6100 The Clery Act Privacy Policy Title IX © 2025 North Carolina Central University To ensure the security of your data, you will be logged out due to inactivity in 3 minutes at . Any data not saved will be lost. Click 'OK' to keep your session active."
