    "https://jobs.nccu.edu/postings/36988": {
      "title": "Assistant/Associate Professor - Accounting",
      "description": "North Carolina Central University Applicant Portal | Assistant/Associate Professor - Accounting Skip to Main Content Toggle navigation Home Search Jobs Log In /Create Account Help Benefits Clery Report Equal Employment Opportunity Assistant/Associate Professor - Accounting Bookmark this Posting Print Preview | Apply for this Job Please see Special Instructions for more details. Criminal background check required Posting Details To create a Posting, first complete the information on this screen, then click the Next button or select the page in the left hand navigation menu. Proceed through all sections and complete all necessary information. To submit the Posting to the next approval step, you must go to the Posting Summary page by clicking on the Next button until you reach the Summary page, or you can select the Summary page link from the left navigation menu. Once the Summary page appears, hover your mouse over the orange Take Action on Posting button for a list of possible approval step options. Position Information Working Title Assistant/Associate Professor - Accounting Position Number F611013 Appointment Type Tenure Track - Initial 2 years FTE 1=9/10 month -Faculty only Position Overview Be an Eagle - Where Purpose Takes Flight! Are you ready to make an impact? At North Carolina Central University ( NCCU ), we are more than an institution—we are a community rooted in a legacy of excellence and transformation. A historically Black university located in Durham, North Carolina, also known as ‘The City of Medicine,’ NCCU has been a cornerstone of education since 1910, fostering innovation and progress. Join our team and enjoy a comprehensive benefits package and exclusive perks designed to support your work-life balance. At NCCU , your professional growth will be nurtured, and your contributions will help shape the future for our students and the community we serve. Become part of a legacy that drives change and achievement. An opportunity awaits you at NCCU , where your purpose can take flight. Visit NCCU .edu . Primary Function of Organizational Unit North Carolina Central University ( NCCU is a Historically Black College or University ( HBCU ) with a mission to prepare students to succeed in the global marketplace. We are consistently ranked as a top HBCU in the South by U.S News & World Report. NCCU Business is a flagship program with majors in Accounting, Business Management ( Finance, Human Resources, Marketing, Management, Real Estate, and Entrepreneurship) Computer Information Systems, Information Technology (Data Analytics, Cyber Security, and Information Communications Technology), and Hospitality & Tourism Administration. We offer BBA and MBA degrees within the School of Business. Our Program is accredited by AACSB (Association to Advanced Collegiate Schools of Business), considered the gold standard. NCCU’S School of Business has an enrollment of over 1,200 students in its undergraduate and graduate programs. The Department of Accounting has an enrollment of approximately 85 undergraduate students. The department has faculty members who have published in peer-reviewed journals, such as The Accounting Review, Contemporary Accounting Research, Accounting, Organizations and Society, Strategic Management Journal, Journal of Business Research, and Journal of Accounting and Public Policy. Additional information about the School of Business is available at: http://www.nccu.edu/academics/sc/business/index.cfm. Primary Purpose of Position The School of Business at North Carolina Central University seeks highly qualified applicants for a 9-month, tenure-track position of Assistant/Associate Professor of Accounting in the Department of Accounting. Selected candidate must include an earned Ph.D. in Business with a Major in Accounting from an AACSB -accredited institution and demonstrated potential for quality teaching and research. ABD candidates from AACSB -accredited universities may be considered at the instructor level. Candidates with teaching interests in accounting systems/data analytics and tax. Candidates with experience using SAP are preferred. Instructional duties include teaching, curriculum development, and participation in the program’s assurance of learning efforts, and may consist of online instruction. In addition to instructional responsibilities, faculty members are expected to maintain an active program of scholarship as well as participate in service activities. Quality productivity in academic research is expected . Exhibit a desire to teach at the undergraduate level, but may also be required to teach graduate courses. Required Knowledge, Skills, and Abilities Teaching interests in accounting systems/data analytics and tax. Experience using SAP is preferred. Instructional duties include teaching, curriculum development, and participation in the program’s assurance of learning efforts, and may consist of online instruction. In addition to instructional responsibilities, faculty members are expected to maintain an active program of scholarship as well as participate in service activities. Quality productivity in academic research is expected . Exhibit a desire to teach at the undergraduate level, but may also be required to teach graduate courses. Minimum Education/Experience The requirements for this position must include an earned Ph.D. in Business with a Major in Accounting from an AACSB -accredited institution and demonstrated potential for quality teaching and research. ABD candidates from AACSB -accredited universities may be considered at the instructor level, but the Assistant Professor position requires completing all doctoral requirements by August 1, 2026. Preference will be given to candidates with relevant teaching and professional business experience with professional certification(s). We invite candidates with teaching interests in accounting systems/data analytics and tax. Candidates with experience using SAP are preferred. Licenses or Certification required by Statute or Regulation N/A Equal Opportunity Employer North Carolina Central University is an equal opportunity and affirmative action employer. All qualified applicants will receive consideration for employment without regard to age, color, disability, gender, gender expression, gender identity, genetic information, national origin, race, religion, sex, sexual orientation, or status as a protected veteran. Key Responsibilities and Related Competencies Function Instructional Describe the specific tasks and responsibilities related to the function. Faculty will focus on teaching, research, service and alignment with the mission of the School of Business. Primary teaching responsibilities include undergraduate courses and maybe required to teach graduate courses in Accounting. Prepared to teach face-to-face and online environments and have evidence of teaching effectiveness. Function Research Describe the specific tasks and responsibilities related to the function. Demonstrate a track record or the potential for producing publications necessary for the School to meet current AACSB International accreditationstandards. Function Public Service Describe the specific tasks and responsibilities related to the function. Service to the School, University, profession and community is also expected. Posting Detail Information Posting Number F000243 Open Date 06/02/2026 Close Date Open Until Filled Yes Date Position Available 08/01/2026 Special Instructions to Applicants Criminal background check required Applicant Documents Required Documents Resume/CV Cover Letter Teaching Philosophy Writing Sample Unofficial Transcripts (official required from selected candidate) List of References Optional Documents Other Document DD-214 (Veterans Only) Licenses and/or Certification required by Statute or Regulation Supplemental Questions Required fields are indicated with an asterisk (*). North Carolina Central University 1801 Fayetteville St. Durham, NC, 27707 Mainline: 919-530-6100 The Clery Act Privacy Policy Title IX © 2025 North Carolina Central University To ensure the security of your data, you will be logged out due to inactivity in 3 minutes at . Any data not saved will be lost. Click 'OK' to keep your session active."
