    "https://jobs.nccu.edu/postings/38535": {
      "title": "Clinical Instructor – Entrepreneurship / Executive Director, Center for Entrepreneurship and Economic Development (CEED)",
      "description": "North Carolina Central University Applicant Portal | Clinical Instructor – Entrepreneurship / Executive Director, Center for Entrepreneurship and Economic Development (CEED) Skip to Main Content Toggle navigation Home Search Jobs Log In /Create Account Help Benefits Clery Report Equal Employment Opportunity Clinical Instructor – Entrepreneurship / Executive Director, Center for Entrepreneurship and Economic Development (CEED) Bookmark this Posting Print Preview | Apply for this Job Please see Special Instructions for more details. Final candidates are subject to criminal background checks, and education/license verification prior to employment. Posting Details To create a Posting, first complete the information on this screen, then click the Next button or select the page in the left hand navigation menu. Proceed through all sections and complete all necessary information. To submit the Posting to the next approval step, you must go to the Posting Summary page by clicking on the Next button until you reach the Summary page, or you can select the Summary page link from the left navigation menu. Once the Summary page appears, hover your mouse over the orange Take Action on Posting button for a list of possible approval step options. Position Information Working Title Clinical Instructor – Entrepreneurship / Executive Director, Center for Entrepreneurship and Economic Development (CEED) Position Number F611032 Appointment Type Fixed Term: 1 year FTE .75 = 40 hours/week, 9 months Position Overview Be an Eagle - Where Purpose Takes Flight! Are you ready to make an impact? At North Carolina Central University ( NCCU ), we are more than an institution—we are a community rooted in a legacy of excellence and transformation. A historically Black university located in Durham, North Carolina, also known as ‘The City of Medicine,’ NCCU has been a cornerstone of education since 1910, fostering innovation and progress. Join our team and enjoy a comprehensive benefits package and exclusive perks designed to support your work-life balance. At NCCU , your professional growth will be nurtured, and your contributions will help shape the future for our students and the community we serve. Become part of a legacy that drives change and achievement. An opportunity awaits you at NCCU , where your purpose can take flight. Visit NCCU .edu . Primary Function of Organizational Unit North Carolina Central University ( NCCU is a Historically Black College or University ( HBCU ) with a mission to prepare students to succeed in the global marketplace. We are consistently ranked as a top HBCU in the South by U.S News & World Report. NCCU Business is a flagship program with majors in Accounting, Business Management (Finance, Human Resources, Marketing, Management, Real Estate, and Entrepreneurship) Computer Information Systems, Information Technology (Data Analytics, Cyber Security, and Information Communications Technology), and Hospitality & Tourism Administration. We offer BBA and MBA degrees within the School of Business. Our Program is accredited by AACSB , considered the goldstandard. NCCU’S School of Business has an enrollment of over 1,200 students in its undergraduate and graduate programs. The department has faculty members who have published in peer-reviewed journals. Additional information about the School of Business is available at: http://www.nccu.edu/academics/sc/business/index.cfm. Primary Purpose of Position The School of Business at North Carolina Central University seeks highly qualified applicants for a 9-month, Clinical Instructor of Entrepreneurship who will also serve as Executive Director of the Center for Entrepreneurship and Economic Development ( CEED ). The successful candidate will teach undergraduate and graduate courses in entrepreneurship and related business disciplines while providing strategic leadership for CEED through the development and administration of innovative academic, co-curricular, and community engagement initiatives that promote entrepreneurship, innovation, and economic development. The qualified candidate must have earned Ph.D. in Entrepreneurship or a related field from an AACSB -accredited program or an equally relevant accredited program in a related discipline. Candidates with a Master’s degree and significant working experience in the entrepreneurship area will also be considered. The Executive Director will work collaboratively with faculty, students, alumni, corporate partners, community organizations, and governmental agencies to advance the mission and strategic goals of the School of Business and the University. Required Knowledge, Skills, and Abilities Responsibilities include teaching undergraduate and graduate courses in entrepreneurship and related business disciplines. Faculty will engage students in the study and application of entrepreneurship, innovation, new venture creation, entrepreneurial finance, small business management, and economic development through experiential learning and applied business practices. While the School’s primary focus is teaching, maintenance of academic qualifications includes continuous scholarly productivity in discipline-related quality journals and/or sustained professional engagement consistent with AACSB standards. Service activities include selected committee assignments at the departmental, School, and/or University levels. The successful candidate must demonstrate excellent oral, written, and interpersonal communication skills; effective problem-solving, diplomacy, and leadership abilities; a demonstrated ability to work collaboratively and develop productive relationships with students, faculty, alumni, entrepreneurs, industry partners, and community stakeholders; and a commitment to maintaining high professional standards and integrity. The candidate should also possess the ability to develop and manage entrepreneurship programs, foster innovation, secure external partnerships and funding opportunities, and provide strategic leadership for the Center for Entrepreneurship and Economic Development. Minimum Education/Experience The qualified candidate must have earned Ph.D. in Entrepreneurship or a related field from an AACSB -accredited program or an equally relevant accredited program in a related discipline. Candidates with a Master’s degree and significant working experience in the entrepreneurship area will also be considered. Licenses or Certification required by Statute or Regulation N/A Equal Opportunity Employer North Carolina Central University is an equal opportunity and affirmative action employer. All qualified applicants will receive consideration for employment without regard to age, color, disability, gender, gender expression, gender identity, genetic information, national origin, race, religion, sex, sexual orientation, or status as a protected veteran. Key Responsibilities and Related Competencies Function Instructional Describe the specific tasks and responsibilities related to the function. Faculty will focus on teaching, scholarly engagement, service, and alignment with the mission of the School of Business. Primary teaching responsibilities include undergraduate and graduate courses in Entrepreneurship and related business disciplines. Responsibilities include teaching in face-to-face and online environments, advising and mentoring students, participating in curriculum development and assessment activities, and maintaining academic qualifications through continuous scholarly and professional engagement. Function Administrative Describe the specific tasks and responsibilities related to the function. Serve as Executive Director of the Center for Entrepreneurship and Economic Development by providing strategic vision and leadership for the Center; developing and expanding entrepreneurship programming across the University; fostering innovation and entrepreneurial culture among students, faculty, and the community; building partnerships with industry, government, nonprofit organizations, and alumni; managing external grants and donor-supported initiatives; organizing entrepreneurship competitions, workshops, incubator activities, and outreach programs; coordinating advisory board activities; pursuing external funding opportunities; representing CEED at university and community events; and ensuring effective administration of the Center in support of the School’s strategic priorities. Function Public Service Describe the specific tasks and responsibilities related to the function. Provide service to the School, University, profession, and community through committee participation, professional engagement, community outreach, mentorship, and activities that advance entrepreneurship, economic development, and the mission of North Carolina Central University. Posting Detail Information Posting Number F000320 Open Date 10/07/2026 Close Date Open Until Filled Yes Date Position Available 07/01/2027 Special Instructions to Applicants Final candidates are subject to criminal background checks, and education/license verification prior to employment. Applicant Documents Required Documents Resume/CV Cover Letter Teaching Philosophy Unofficial Transcripts (official required from selected candidate) List of References Optional Documents Other Document DD-214 (Veterans Only) NGB23A or NGB22/DD256 (National Guard Only) Licenses and/or Certification required by Statute or Regulation Supplemental Questions Required fields are indicated with an asterisk (*). North Carolina Central University 1801 Fayetteville St. Durham, NC, 27707 Mainline: 919-530-6100 The Clery Act Privacy Policy Title IX © 2025 North Carolina Central University To ensure the security of your data, you will be logged out due to inactivity in 3 minutes at . Any data not saved will be lost. Click 'OK' to keep your session active."
    },
    "https://jobs.nccu.edu/postings/38582": {
      "title": "Clinical Associate Professor",
      "description": "North Carolina Central University Applicant Portal | Clinical Associate Professor Skip to Main Content Toggle navigation Home Search Jobs Log In /Create Account Help Benefits Clery Report Equal Employment Opportunity Clinical Associate Professor Bookmark this Posting Print Preview | Apply for this Job Please see Special Instructions for more details. Final candidates are subject to criminal background checks, and education/license verification prior to employment. Posting Details To create a Posting, first complete the information on this screen, then click the Next button or select the page in the left hand navigation menu. Proceed through all sections and complete all necessary information. To submit the Posting to the next approval step, you must go to the Posting Summary page by clicking on the Next button until you reach the Summary page, or you can select the Summary page link from the left navigation menu. Once the Summary page appears, hover your mouse over the orange Take Action on Posting button for a list of possible approval step options. Position Information Working Title Clinical Associate Professor Position Number F610388 Appointment Type Permanent - Full Time FTE 1=9/10 month -Faculty only Position Overview Be an Eagle - Where Purpose Takes Flight! Are you ready to make an impact? At North Carolina Central University ( NCCU ), we are more than an institution—we are a community rooted in a legacy of excellence and transformation. A historically Black university located in Durham, North Carolina, also known as ‘The City of Medicine,’ NCCU has been a cornerstone of education since 1910, fostering innovation and progress. Join our team and enjoy a comprehensive benefits package and exclusive perks designed to support your work-life balance. At NCCU , your professional growth will be nurtured, and your contributions will help shape the future for our students and the community we serve. Become part of a legacy that drives change and achievement. An opportunity awaits you at NCCU , where your purpose can take flight. Visit NCCU .edu . Primary Function of Organizational Unit The primary purpose of the Department of Psychology is to provide undergraduate and graduate students rigorous training in the understanding of human behavior using scientific methods, and to provide students with the competencies, knowledge and skills sufficient to: (1) qualify for graduate/doctoral studies in psychology and the behavioral sciences and; (2) qualify for a range of human service positions that require the application of psychological or behavioral science methods and skills. Primary Purpose of Position The primary purpose of this Clinical Associate faculty position is to teach in the undergraduate and/or the graduate programs, serve as an advisor, conduct research, engage in service to the unit, and contribute to the development of the Department of Psychology. Required Knowledge, Skills, and Abilities Licensed psychologist Ability to teach undergraduate courses and applied courses in the clinical concentration of the graduate program; supervise students on practicum; conduct research; serve as a thesis advisor in the graduate program Minimum Education/Experience Earned Master’s or PHD in related field. Licenses or Certification required by Statute or Regulation Licensed Psychologist/licensable in North Carolina Equal Opportunity Employer North Carolina Central University is an equal opportunity and affirmative action employer. All qualified applicants will receive consideration for employment without regard to age, color, disability, gender, gender expression, gender identity, genetic information, national origin, race, religion, sex, sexual orientation, or status as a protected veteran. Key Responsibilities and Related Competencies Function Instructional Describe the specific tasks and responsibilities related to the function. Teach undergraduate courses and graduate courses in the clinical concentration. Function Research Describe the specific tasks and responsibilities related to the function. Develop and conduct research. Publish peer reviewed journals. Function Administrative Describe the specific tasks and responsibilities related to the function. Performs academic and administrative duties, including developing and maintaining Canvas course shells, preparing and updating course syllabi, submitting grades and required academic documentation, maintaining student records, participating in department and college meetings, serving on committees, advising students, and completing other departmental and university administrative responsibilities as assigned Function Other Duties as Assigned Describe the specific tasks and responsibilities related to the function. Other related administrative, instructional and service tasks as assigned by the department chair. Posting Detail Information Posting Number F000326 Open Date 10/22/2026 Close Date 10/30/2026 Open Until Filled No Date Position Available 01/01/2027 Special Instructions to Applicants Final candidates are subject to criminal background checks, and education/license verification prior to employment. Applicant Documents Required Documents Resume/CV Cover Letter Unofficial Transcripts (official required from selected candidate) Letter of Recommendation 1 Letter of Recommendation 2 Letter of Recommendation 3 List of References Optional Documents Other Document DD-214 (Veterans Only) NGB23A or NGB22/DD256 (National Guard Only) Licenses and/or Certification required by Statute or Regulation Supplemental Questions Required fields are indicated with an asterisk (*). North Carolina Central University 1801 Fayetteville St. Durham, NC, 27707 Mainline: 919-530-6100 The Clery Act Privacy Policy Title IX © 2025 North Carolina Central University To ensure the security of your data, you will be logged out due to inactivity in 3 minutes at . Any data not saved will be lost. Click 'OK' to keep your session active."
