      "description": "North Carolina Central University Applicant Portal | Clinical Instructor - Real Estate / Director of Real Estate Studies Skip to Main Content Toggle navigation Home Search Jobs Log In /Create Account Help Benefits Clery Report Equal Employment Opportunity Clinical Instructor - Real Estate / Director of Real Estate Studies Bookmark this Posting Print Preview | Apply for this Job Please see Special Instructions for more details. Final candidates are subject to criminal background checks, and education/license verification prior to employment. Posting Details To create a Posting, first complete the information on this screen, then click the Next button or select the page in the left hand navigation menu. Proceed through all sections and complete all necessary information. To submit the Posting to the next approval step, you must go to the Posting Summary page by clicking on the Next button until you reach the Summary page, or you can select the Summary page link from the left navigation menu. Once the Summary page appears, hover your mouse over the orange Take Action on Posting button for a list of possible approval step options. Position Information Working Title Clinical Instructor - Real Estate / Director of Real Estate Studies Position Number F611035 Appointment Type Fixed Term: 1 year FTE 1=9/10 month -Faculty only Position Overview Be an Eagle - Where Purpose Takes Flight! Are you ready to make an impact? At North Carolina Central University ( NCCU ), we are more than an institution—we are a community rooted in a legacy of excellence and transformation. A historically Black university located in Durham, North Carolina, also known as ‘The City of Medicine,’ NCCU has been a cornerstone of education since 1910, fostering innovation and progress. Join our team and enjoy a comprehensive benefits package and exclusive perks designed to support your work-life balance. At NCCU , your professional growth will be nurtured, and your contributions will help shape the future for our students and the community we serve. Become part of a legacy that drives change and achievement. An opportunity awaits you at NCCU , where your purpose can take flight. Visit NCCU .edu . Primary Function of Organizational Unit North Carolina Central University ( NCCU is a Historically Black College or University ( HBCU ) with a mission to prepare students to succeed in the global marketplace. We are consistently ranked as a top HBCU in the South by U.S News & World Report. NCCU Business is a flagship program with majors in Accounting, Business Management (Finance, Human Resources, Marketing, Management, Real Estate, and Entrepreneurship) Computer Information Systems, Information Technology (Data Analytics, CyberSecurity, and Information Communications Technology), and Hospitality & Tourism Administration. We offer BBA and MBA degrees within the School of Business. Our Program is accredited by AACSB , considered the gold standard. NCCU’S School of Business has an enrollment of over 1,200 students in its undergraduate and graduate programs. The department has faculty members who have published in peer-reviewed journals. Additional information about the School of Business is available at: http://www.nccu.edu/academics/sc/business/index.cfm. Primary Purpose of Position The School of Business at North Carolina Central University seeks highly qualified applicants for a 9-month, Clinical Instructor of Real Estate who will also serve as Director of the Real Estate Studies. The successful candidate will teach undergraduate and graduate courses in Real Estate and related business disciplines while providing strategic leadership for the Real Estate Studies through the development and administration of innovative academic, co-curricular, and community engagement initiatives that promote Real Estate, innovation, and economic development. The qualified candidate must have earned Ph.D. in Real Estate or a related field from an AACSB -accredited program or an equally relevant accredited program in a related discipline. Candidates with a Master’s degree and significant working experience in the real estate area will also be considered. The Director will work collaboratively with faculty, students, alumni, corporate partners, community organizations, and governmental agencies to advance the mission and strategic goals of the School of Business and the University. Required Knowledge, Skills, and Abilities Responsibilities include teaching undergraduate and graduate courses in real estate and related business disciplines. Faculty will engage students in the study and application of , and economic development through experiential learning and applied business practices. While the School’s primary focus is teaching, maintenance of academic qualifications includes continuous scholarly productivity in discipline-related quality journals and/or sustained professional engagement consistent with AACSB standards. Service activities include selected committee assignments at the departmental, School, and/or University levels. The successful candidate must demonstrate excellent oral, written, and interpersonal communication skills; effective problem-solving, diplomacy, and leadership abilities; a demonstrated ability to work collaboratively and develop productive relationships with students, faculty, alumni, entrepreneurs, industry partners, and community stakeholders; and a commitment to maintaining high professional standards and integrity. The candidate should also possess the ability to develop and manage real estate programs, foster innovation, secure external partnerships and funding opportunities, and provide strategic leadership for the Real Estate Program. Minimum Education/Experience The qualified candidate must have earned Ph.D. in Real Estate or a related field from an AACSB accredited program or an equally relevant accredited program in a related discipline. Candidates with a Master’s degree and significant working experience in the real estate area will also be considered. Licenses or Certification required by Statute or Regulation N/A Equal Opportunity Employer North Carolina Central University is an equal opportunity and affirmative action employer. All qualified applicants will receive consideration for employment without regard to age, color, disability, gender, gender expression, gender identity, genetic information, national origin, race, religion, sex, sexual orientation, or status as a protected veteran. Key Responsibilities and Related Competencies Function Instructional Describe the specific tasks and responsibilities related to the function. Faculty will focus on teaching, scholarly engagement, service, and alignment with the mission of the School of Business. Primary teaching responsibilities include undergraduate and graduate courses in Real Estate and related business disciplines. Responsibilities include teaching in face-to-face and online environments, advising and mentoring students, participating in curriculum development and assessment activities, and maintaining academic qualifications through continuous scholarly and professional engagement Function Administrative Describe the specific tasks and responsibilities related to the function. Serve as Director of the Real Estate Studies by providing strategic vision and leadership for the program; developing and expanding real estate programming across the University; fostering innovation and a real estate ownership among students, faculty, and the community; building partnerships with industry, government, nonprofit organizations, and alumni; managing external grants and donor-supported initiatives; organizing real estate competitions, workshops, incubator activities ,and outreach programs; coordinating advisory board activities; pursuing external funding opportunities; representing the real estate program at university and community events; and ensuring effective administration of the program in support of the School’s strategic priorities. Function Public Service Describe the specific tasks and responsibilities related to the function. Provide service to the School, University, profession, and community through committee participation, professional engagement, community outreach, mentorship, and activities that advance entrepreneurship, economic development, and the mission of North Carolina Central University. Posting Detail Information Posting Number F000321 Open Date 10/15/2026 Close Date Open Until Filled No Date Position Available 07/01/2027 Special Instructions to Applicants Final candidates are subject to criminal background checks, and education/license verification prior to employment. Applicant Documents Required Documents Resume/CV Cover Letter Unofficial Transcripts (official required from selected candidate) List of References Optional Documents Other Document DD-214 (Veterans Only) Licenses and/or Certification required by Statute or Regulation Supplemental Questions Required fields are indicated with an asterisk (*). North Carolina Central University 1801 Fayetteville St. Durham, NC, 27707 Mainline: 919-530-6100 The Clery Act Privacy Policy Title IX © 2025 North Carolina Central University To ensure the security of your data, you will be logged out due to inactivity in 3 minutes at . Any data not saved will be lost. Click 'OK' to keep your session active."
    },
    "https://jobs.nccu.edu/postings/38554": {
      "title": "Assistant Professor - Decision Sciences",
      "description": "North Carolina Central University Applicant Portal | Assistant Professor - Decision Sciences Skip to Main Content Toggle navigation Home Search Jobs Log In /Create Account Help Benefits Clery Report Equal Employment Opportunity Assistant Professor - Decision Sciences Bookmark this Posting Print Preview | Apply for this Job Please see Special Instructions for more details. Final candidates are subject to criminal background checks, and education/license verification prior to employment. Posting Details To create a Posting, first complete the information on this screen, then click the Next button or select the page in the left hand navigation menu. Proceed through all sections and complete all necessary information. To submit the Posting to the next approval step, you must go to the Posting Summary page by clicking on the Next button until you reach the Summary page, or you can select the Summary page link from the left navigation menu. Once the Summary page appears, hover your mouse over the orange Take Action on Posting button for a list of possible approval step options. Position Information Working Title Assistant Professor - Decision Sciences Position Number F611257 Appointment Type Tenure Track - Initial 2 years FTE .75 = 40 hours/week, 9 months Position Overview Be an Eagle - Where Purpose Takes Flight! Are you ready to make an impact? At North Carolina Central University ( NCCU ), we are more than an institution—we are a community rooted in a legacy of excellence and transformation. A historically Black university located in Durham, North Carolina, also known as ‘The City of Medicine,’ NCCU has been a cornerstone of education since 1910, fostering innovation and progress. Join our team and enjoy a comprehensive benefits package and exclusive perks designed to support your work-life balance. At NCCU , your professional growth will be nurtured, and your contributions will help shape the future for our students and the community we serve. Become part of a legacy that drives change and achievement. An opportunity awaits you at NCCU , where your purpose can take flight. Visit NCCU .edu . Primary Function of Organizational Unit North Carolina Central University ( NCCU is a Historically Black College or University ( HBCU ) with a mission to prepare students to succeed in the global marketplace. We are consistently ranked as a top HBCU in the South by U.S News & World Report. NCCU Business is a flagship program with majors in Accounting, Business Administration ( Financial Analytics, Human Resources, Marketing, Management, Real Estate, and Entrepreneurship) Computer Information Systems, Information Technology (Data Analytics, Cyber Security, and Information Communications and Technology), and Hospitality & Tourism Administration. We offer BBA and MBA degrees within the School of Business. Our Program is accredited by AACSB (Association to Advanced Collegiate Schools of Business), considered the gold standard. NCCU’S School of Business has an enrollment of over 1,200 students in its undergraduate and graduate programs. The department has faculty members who have published in peer-reviewed journals. Additional information about the School of Business is available at: http://www.nccu.edu/academics/sc/business/index.cfm. Primary Purpose of Position The School of Business at North Carolina Central University seeks highly qualified applicants for a 9-month, tenure-track position of Assistant Professor of Decision Sciences in the Department of Decision Sciences. Selected candidate must have earned Ph.D. in statistics or related field from an AACSB -accredited institution and demonstrated potential for quality teaching and research. ABD candidates from AACSB -accredited universities may be considered at the instructor level. Candidates with teaching interests in statistical computing, data analytics, and quantitative methods at the undergraduate and graduate levels. Instructional duties include teaching, curriculum development, and participation in the program’s assurance of learning efforts, and may consist of online instruction. In addition to instructional responsibilities, faculty members are expected to maintain an active program of scholarship as well as participate in service activities. Quality productivity in academic research is expected . Exhibit a desire to teach at the undergraduate level, but may also be required to teach graduate courses. Required Knowledge, Skills, and Abilities Teaching statistics, statistical computing, data analytics, and quantitative methods at the undergraduate and graduate levels, and conducting research. Excellent oral, written, and interpersonal communication skills; effective problem solving, diplomacy, and leadership skills; demonstrated ability to work as part of a team and develop productive working relationships with multiple stakeholders; a commitment to overall high standards and professional integrity. Minimum Education/Experience The qualified candidate must have an earned Ph.D. in statistics or a related field from an AACSB accredited program or equally relevant accredited program in a related discipline and demonstrated potential for quality teaching and research. Teaching experience in regression analysis, categorical data, applied time series, optimization, statistical computing using R and SAS is highly desirable. Licenses or Certification required by Statute or Regulation N/A Equal Opportunity Employer North Carolina Central University is an equal opportunity and affirmative action employer. All qualified applicants will receive consideration for employment without regard to age, color, disability, gender, gender expression, gender identity, genetic information, national origin, race, religion, sex, sexual orientation, or status as a protected veteran. Key Responsibilities and Related Competencies Function Instructional Describe the specific tasks and responsibilities related to the function. Faculty will focus on teaching, research, service and alignment with the mission of the School of Business. Primary teaching responsibilities include undergraduate courses and maybe required to teach graduate courses in Decision Sciences. Prepared to teach face-to-face and online environments and have evidence of teaching effectiveness. Function Research Describe the specific tasks and responsibilities related to the function. Demonstrate a track record or the potential for producing publications necessary for the School to meet current AACSB International accreditation standards. Function Public Service Describe the specific tasks and responsibilities related to the function. Service to the School, University, profession and community is also expected. Posting Detail Information Posting Number F000319 Open Date 10/07/2026 Close Date Open Until Filled Yes Date Position Available 07/01/2027 Special Instructions to Applicants Final candidates are subject to criminal background checks, and education/license verification prior to employment. Applicant Documents Required Documents Resume/CV Cover Letter Teaching Philosophy Unofficial Transcripts (official required from selected candidate) List of References Optional Documents Other Document DD-214 (Veterans Only) NGB23A or NGB22/DD256 (National Guard Only) Licenses and/or Certification required by Statute or Regulation Supplemental Questions Required fields are indicated with an asterisk (*). North Carolina Central University 1801 Fayetteville St. Durham, NC, 27707 Mainline: 919-530-6100 The Clery Act Privacy Policy Title IX © 2025 North Carolina Central University To ensure the security of your data, you will be logged out due to inactivity in 3 minutes at . Any data not saved will be lost. Click 'OK' to keep your session active."
    },
    "https://jobs.nccu.edu/postings/38611": {
      "title": "Adjunct Instructor-Mass Communication",
      "description": "North Carolina Central University Applicant Portal | Adjunct Instructor-Mass Communication Skip to Main Content Toggle navigation Home Search Jobs Log In /Create Account Help Benefits Clery Report Equal Employment Opportunity Adjunct Instructor-Mass Communication Bookmark this Posting Print Preview | Apply for this Job Please see Special Instructions for more details. Final candidates are subject to criminal background checks, and education/license verification prior to employment. Posting Details To create a Posting, first complete the information on this screen, then click the Next button or select the page in the left hand navigation menu. Proceed through all sections and complete all necessary information. To submit the Posting to the next approval step, you must go to the Posting Summary page by clicking on the Next button until you reach the Summary page, or you can select the Summary page link from the left navigation menu. Once the Summary page appears, hover your mouse over the orange Take Action on Posting button for a list of possible approval step options. Position Information Working Title Adjunct Instructor-Mass Communication Position Number FA9976 Appointment Type By semester: Spring FTE 1=9/10 month -Faculty only Position Overview Be an Eagle - Where Purpose Takes Flight! Are you ready to make an impact? At North Carolina Central University ( NCCU ), we are more than an institution—we are a community rooted in a legacy of excellence and transformation. A historically Black university located in Durham, North Carolina, also known as ‘The City of Medicine,’ NCCU has been a cornerstone of education since 1910, fostering innovation and progress. Join our team and enjoy a comprehensive benefits package and exclusive perks designed to support your work-life balance. At NCCU , your professional growth will be nurtured, and your contributions will help shape the future for our students and the community we serve. Become part of a legacy that drives change and achievement. An opportunity awaits you at NCCU , where your purpose can take flight. Visit NCCU .edu . Primary Function of Organizational Unit The mission of the Department of Mass Communication is to prepare students for careers and study in mass communication. The department offers engaged learning, student media and research experiences and connections to professional practice opportunities. The department values the comprehensive preparation of graduates with a strong foundation in the ethical, practical, and theoretical aspects of the field that foster an appreciation for the varied perspectives and backgrounds that enrich our global society. Primary Purpose of Position The adjunct instructor will be responsible for teaching courses in the department as assigned. The responsibilities of instructors include teaching, evaluation, and other instruction-related duties and responsibilities that help the department achieve its mission and meet the goals of the University, including the following: Holding office hours Setting up assignments Setting up grading policies and procedures Creating the course syllabus Learning the University’s Canvas course management system Reporting midterm and final grades by specified deadlines Communicating problems in your courses to the department chair Engaging in teaching-focused professional development Receiving annual peer-teaching reviews Contributing to department assessment efforts Having students complete Student Ratings of Instruction ( SRI ) surveys each semester Required Knowledge, Skills, and Abilities Knowledge of principles and methods for curriculum and training design in mass communication or related fields as appropriate to the assigned course(s). Knowledge of appropriate strategies for teaching and instruction for individuals and groups. Knowledge of appropriate strategies for the measurement of instructional outcomes. Knowledge of media production, communication, and dissemination techniques and methods, including alternative ways to inform and entertain via written, oral, and visual media. An understanding of appropriate learning strategies as well as problem-solving and organizational skills. Willingness to engage in teaching-related professional development activities. Ability to communicate effectively both orally and in writing. Ability to maintain office hours as required. Minimum Education/Experience Master’s degree in mass communication or communication is required. A master’s degree in a closely related academic field may be considered if the degree provides a foundation for an extensive record of professional achievement and significant professional experience in mass communication, speech communication, and/or digital and new media, as appropriate to the assigned course(s). Licenses or Certification required by Statute or Regulation Not applicable Equal Opportunity Employer North Carolina Central University is an equal opportunity and affirmative action employer. All qualified applicants will receive consideration for employment without regard to age, color, disability, gender, gender expression, gender identity, genetic information, national origin, race, religion, sex, sexual orientation, or status as a protected veteran. Key Responsibilities and Related Competencies Posting Detail Information Posting Number F000327 Open Date 10/29/2026 Close Date 11/30/2026 Open Until Filled No Date Position Available 10/20/2026 Special Instructions to Applicants Final candidates are subject to criminal background checks, and education/license verification prior to employment. Applicant Documents Required Documents Resume/CV Cover Letter Unofficial Transcripts (official required from selected candidate) List of References Optional Documents Teaching Philosophy Other Document DD-214 (Veterans Only) NGB23A or NGB22/DD256 (National Guard Only) Licenses and/or Certification required by Statute or Regulation Supplemental Questions Required fields are indicated with an asterisk (*). North Carolina Central University 1801 Fayetteville St. Durham, NC, 27707 Mainline: 919-530-6100 The Clery Act Privacy Policy Title IX © 2025 North Carolina Central University To ensure the security of your data, you will be logged out due to inactivity in 3 minutes at . Any data not saved will be lost. Click 'OK' to keep your session active."
